{#
  The backdrop, and the clock.

  A fixed page of prompter script sits behind everything and drifts upward as
  you scroll — the site is a teleprompter you are reading down. The lines are
  written by script.js rather than by this template, deliberately: text set at
  five per cent contrast has no business being in the HTML where it would read
  as hidden copy, and with no JavaScript the page is simply white, which is
  what it should be anyway.

  The clock is the one in the app, in the corner it lives in there. It counts
  how long you have been on the page and stops when you press it.
#}
<div class="prompter-bg" aria-hidden="true" data-prompter-bg>
    <div class="prompter-bg-inner" data-prompter-lines></div>
</div>

<button class="stopwatch" type="button" data-stopwatch
        aria-label="Reading timer — press to pause">
    <i class="stopwatch-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i>
    <span class="stopwatch-time" data-stopwatch-time>00:00</span>
    <span class="stopwatch-label">On air</span>
</button>
